- Precedence & convergence layout (`c1`, `c2`, nested branching): Distorts intended chronology and path progression (SMC3/SMC4/SMC5). The model artificially splits a single ternary choice into multiple levels and routes non-existent "No" branches through `converge(c1)` to the hallucinated early end, breaking the exact sequence "check mismatches → choose option → continue → park invoice → end" described in the text.